-- CONTROL — IT BOUNDS Q1's SCOPE. A method name shared with the PRELUDE must still
-- be ACCEPTED, and must be invariant under interface-declaration order.
--
-- ⭐ WHY THIS CONTROL, AND WHAT IT REPLACED. Until Q1 (Stage B / Phase 4b) this slot
-- held control-shared-method-name-disjoint-receivers/: two interfaces in this file
-- both declaring `n`, with impls at DISJOINT receivers, asserted invariant. Q1
-- rejects that shape ON THE DECLARATION, so it can no longer be written here at all
-- -- and it is NOT re-posed elsewhere, because it is inexpressible. MEASURED, four
-- ways, on a binary built from this branch:
--   * both interfaces in THIS module          -> R-DUPLICATE-IFACE-METHOD (Q1);
--   * this module's interface + an IMPORTED one -> the module's own declaration wins
--     the name and the imported method is unreachable (`No impl of E1 for V`), so
--     the second receiver cannot be observed;
--   * two IMPORTED modules                    -> `Ambiguous occurrence: 'n' is
--     exported by both `pu` and `pv``, already rejected before Q1;
--   * this module's interface + the PRELUDE   -> the prelude side is shadowed and
--     unreachable too (`No impl of Floor for Int`).
-- So "one method name observed at two receivers" only ever existed in the first
-- case, which is exactly what Q1 removes. See the PR for the transcripts.
--
-- ⭐ WHAT THIS ONE ASSERTS INSTEAD, and why it is the sharp control now: Q1's scope
-- ruling is that the PRELUDE IS OUT (docs/spec/SHADOW-SEMANTICS.md S1-PRELUDE, held
-- by #1499 under the reserved `W-PRELUDE-METHOD-SHADOW`). `Floor` declares
-- `minBound`, which is core's `Bounded.minBound` -- a live prelude interface method
-- with prelude impls. If Q1 ever seeds itself from the prelude, THIS FILE STOPS
-- COMPILING and the row goes red. That is the only in-tree guard on that boundary.
--
-- how-established: not read off the engine. `minBound` here can only be `U` (it is
-- the argument of `useU : U -> Int`), and `tag U` can only be `impl Tag U`; no
-- ranking between interfaces is performed in either, so the answer is 4 + 5 = 9 in
-- every ordering. `minBound` was chosen over `eq`/`map`/`hash` because those three
-- break the prelude's OWN bodies at exit 1 today (a pre-existing #1499-adjacent
-- residue, measured), which would make this control assert a failure rather than an
-- acceptance.
interface Floor a where
  minBound : a

interface Tag a where
  tag : a -> Int

data U = U

impl Floor U where
  minBound = U

impl Tag U where
  tag _ = 4

useU : U -> Int
useU u = tag u + 5

main = println (useU minBound)
